window.AG_CHAPTERS["20"] = {"id":"20","title":"The Side of His Head","titleZh":"頭之一側","patient":{"name":"Liu Qi the wheelwright 車匠柳七","sprite":"man"},"scene":{"img":"art/scene-treatment.jpg","key":"rain"},"pattern":"Blood Stasis Headache on the Shaoyang Channel 瘀血頭痛 · 少陽經","principle":"invigorate blood, free the network vessels, and free the channel where the pain actually sits","tongue":"dark purple with stasis patches, the coating thin and unremarkable","pulseNote":{"en":"Fine, and rough with it — the beat does not glide, it drags.","zh":"細而兼澀，其至不利而滯"},"needleAsk":{"en":"Needle <b>Shu&#242;g&#468; GB8</b>. Tap its exact location.","zh":"行針 — 點出穴位精確位置"},"target":{"id":"GB8","zh":"率谷","py":"Shu&#242;g&#468;","x":232,"y":340,"img":"art/body-head-lateral.jpg","w":434,"h":1159,"view":{"x":130,"y":238,"w":230,"h":300},"decoys":[{"x":232,"y":272},{"x":186,"y":414},{"x":288,"y":396},{"x":232,"y":414},{"x":150,"y":432}],"note":"<b>率谷 Shu&#242;g&#468; GB8</b> — directly above the apex of the ear, one and a half cun within the hairline. A Gallbladder point on the side of the head and a meeting point with the Bladder channel; the local point of choice for one-sided headache and for pain over the temporal region.<br>耳尖直上，入髮際一寸半。足少陽膽經，與足太陽交會。偏頭痛、顳部疼痛之局部要穴。"},"hints":{"ask":{"en":"Ask him to put one finger where it hurts. The <b>place</b> is the first diagnosis.","zh":"令其以一指指所痛之處。其<b>部位</b>即第一診。"},"look":{"en":"The coating tells you almost nothing here. Look past it, at the body of the tongue.","zh":"本案之苔幾無所告。當越苔而觀其質。"},"pulse":{"en":"Two qualities. One says how much blood there is; the other says how well it travels.","zh":"脈見二象：一言血之多寡，一言血之利否。"},"dx":{"en":"Which channel, then what kind of pain, then rule out the three that look like it.","zh":"先定何經，次辨其性，末排三似證。"},"rx":{"en":"One point on the painful side, right where he put his finger. Then a point far away that moves blood upward.","zh":"一穴取其痛側，正在其指所指之處；一穴取遠道，以行血上達。"},"tech":{"en":"Eight months in one spot, refusing pressure. Nothing here is short.","zh":"八月而止一處，且拒按。本案無所不足。"}},"reactions":[{"who":"master","en":"Master Shen watches which hand the man raises, and where it goes.","zh":"參師父看他抬的是哪隻手，以及手往何處去。"},{"who":"patient","en":"Liu Qi presses two fingers above his right ear and leaves them there while he talks.","zh":"柳七以二指按右耳之上，說話時一直按著。"},{"who":"boy","en":"The herb boy has been sent for the ink block twice and forgotten twice.","zh":"藥童取墨去了兩趟，兩趟都忘了。"},{"who":"master","en":"\"He has told you the channel without knowing the word for it. Which one?\"","zh":"「他已把經告訴你了，只是不知其名。是何經？」"},{"who":"patient","en":"\"Eight months. Since the shaft came down on me.\"","zh":"「八個月了。自從那根車轅砸下來。」"},{"who":"master","en":"\"An injury, a fixed spot, and a face that colour. You already know. Prove it.\"","zh":"「有傷、有定處、而面色如此。你心中已知，且證之。」"}],"remedy":{"ask":"pain_quality","look":"cold_heat","pulse":"cold_heat","dx":"channel_organ","rx":"channel_organ","tech":"excess_def"},"reward":{"cardEn":"Where the Pain Sits Names the Channel","cardZh":"頭痛分經 · 血瘀阻絡","cardTxt":"Headache is one of the few complaints where the location alone narrows the answer, because the channels divide the head between them. Back of the head running into the nape is Taiyang. Forehead and brow-ridge is Yangming. Both sides, temple to ear, is Shaoyang. The vertex, and pain drawing into the eye, is Jueyin. Name the channel from the place, then name the pathology from the quality — stabbing, fixed, worse at night, after an injury, with a purple tongue is blood stasis — and the two together give you a local point and a prescription at the same time.","herbId":"chuanxiong","herbEn":"Chuanxiong Rhizome","herbZh":"川芎","herbImg":"art/card-chuanxiong.jpg","sprite":"art/sprite-renshen-jump.webp","herbTxt":"Acrid and warm, entering Liver, Gallbladder and Pericardium. Called the qi-herb within the blood: it moves blood and moves qi at the same time, which is why it is in almost every blood-moving formula. It also rises — it reaches the head, and the old line is that no headache formula is without it. Being acrid, warm and dispersing, it is used cautiously in yin deficiency with heat, in heavy menstrual bleeding, and in pregnancy."},"endings":{"three":["Two months on, Liu Qi says the nights are his own again. \"I did not think anything could be done after this long,\" he says.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You named the channel from where his finger went, and the pathology from how he described it. Those are two different questions and most students only ask one.\"","二月後，柳七言夜已復為己有。「拖了這麼久，我以為沒治了。」<br><b>參師父：</b>「你由其指之所指而定其經，由其言之所狀而定其理。此二問也，而學者多只問其一。」"],"two":["The pain is duller and comes less often. It still finds him at night.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You had the channel. Go back to the quality of the pain — you treated it as if it were merely stuck.\"","痛已減而發亦稀，然夜猶尋之。<br><b>參師父：</b>「經已得矣。回頭看痛之性質——你只作滯治之。」"],"one":["He thanks you and puts his fingers back above his ear.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"He pointed at the answer twice. Look at his hand.\"","他道了謝，手指又按回耳上。<br><b>參師父：</b>「他指了兩回。看他的手。」"],"titles":["Liu Qi Sleeps on His Right Side","Liu Qi Has Fewer Bad Nights","Liu Qi Keeps His Hand There"]},"script":[{"w":"master","en":"Headache. Before you think about organs, think about geography — the head is divided between channels.","cn":"頭痛之證。未論臟腑，先論部位——頭之分屬，各有其經。"},{"w":"patient","en":"I build cartwheels. Eight months ago a shaft came loose and caught me here.","cn":"我做車輪。八個月前，一根車轅鬆脫，正砸在這裡。"},{"w":"patient","en":"The bruise went. The pain stayed. Always this side, always this spot.","cn":"瘀青退了，痛沒退。永遠這一側，永遠這一處。"},{"w":"patient","en":"Like a nail going in. Worse after dark. Some nights I cannot lie on that side at all.","cn":"像釘子往裡鑽。天黑之後更甚。有些夜裡，那一側根本不能著枕。"},{"w":"master","en":"A place, a quality, and a history. Ask in that order and the case will fall open.","cn":"部位、性質、病史。依此序而問，其案自解。"}],"qa":[{"q":"Put one finger exactly where it hurts.","cq":"以一指指其確痛之處。","good":1,"a":"He puts two fingers above his right ear and runs them forward to the temple.","ca":"他以二指按右耳之上，復向前劃至太陽穴。","clue":{"en":"Right temporal region, ear to temple","zh":"右側顳部，自耳上至太陽"},"note":"The head is divided between the channels, and location alone eliminates most of the field. Temple to ear, on one or both sides, is <b>Shaoyang</b> — Gallbladder and Triple Burner. Back of the head into the nape is <b>Taiyang</b>. Forehead and brow-ridge is <b>Yangming</b>. The vertex, drawing into the eye, is <b>Jueyin</b>. Ask the patient to point before you ask anything else. 頭分諸經，但憑部位即可去其大半。顳部連耳，一側或兩側者，<b>少陽</b>也（膽與三焦）。後頭連項者<b>太陽</b>。前額連眉稜骨者<b>陽明</b>。巔頂而牽引目系者<b>厥陰</b>。凡問頭痛，先令其指。"},{"q":"What is the pain like?","cq":"其痛何狀？","good":1,"a":"A nail. Going in, and staying in.","ca":"如釘。鑽入而不出。","clue":{"en":"Boring, stabbing pain","zh":"痛如錐鑽"},"note":"Location names the channel; quality names the pathology. Boring or stabbing is blood stasis. Distending is qi or Liver yang. Empty and hollow is deficiency. Heavy, as though the head were wrapped in wet cloth, is damp or phlegm. Two questions, two different axes — and you need both. 部位定其經，性質定其理。刺痛鑽痛者血瘀；脹痛者氣滯或肝陽；空痛者虛；頭重如裹者濕痰。二問各主一軸，缺一不可。"},{"q":"Is it always in the same place?","cq":"其痛常在一處否？","good":1,"a":"Always. Eight months, the same handspan of skull.","ca":"始終如一。八個月，就那一巴掌大的地方。","clue":{"en":"Fixed location for eight months","zh":"痛處固定八月不移"},"note":"Fixed confirms stasis and rules out wind, which wanders. It also separates this from Liver yang rising, where the pain is usually both-sided or at the vertex and varies with mood, sleep and anger rather than staying pinned to one handspan. 固定則證瘀，且排除風邪——風性善行。又足以別於肝陽上亢：彼痛多兩側或在巔，且隨情志、寐、怒而變，不常拘於一掌之地。"},{"q":"Worse at any time of day?","cq":"何時為甚？","good":1,"a":"After dark. And if I have been bent over the lathe all day, worse again.","ca":"入夜。若整日俯身於車床，則又甚。","clue":{"en":"Worse at night and after prolonged posture","zh":"入夜及久俯後尤甚"},"note":"Night is yin; blood is yin and slows as yang withdraws, so stasis pain sharpens after dark. This is the same marker you met in chapter eighteen, in a different part of the body — which is the point: a pathology behaves the same way wherever it sits. 夜屬陰，血亦屬陰；陽入而血行緩，故瘀痛入夜而劇。此與第十八章所見同一標記，特其部位異耳——病理不易其性，隨處皆然。"},{"q":"Does pressing it help?","cq":"按之減否？","good":1,"a":"No. I press it because I cannot help it, not because it helps.","ca":"不減。我按著是忍不住，不是因為按了好些。","clue":{"en":"Refuses pressure","zh":"拒按"},"note":"An excellent answer to catch, because his hand has been on his head throughout the consultation and you might have read that as <i>likes pressure</i>. Ask; do not infer. Refusing pressure marks excess, and it rules out the empty, hollow headache of blood deficiency, where a warm hand genuinely helps. 此答尤當留意：其手自診始即按於頭，若但憑所見，幾誤以為喜按。當問而勿臆。拒按者屬實，且排除血虛之空痛——彼則得溫手按之而誠減。"},{"q":"Tell me about the injury.","cq":"言其受傷之事。","good":1,"a":"The shaft came down on the right side of my head. I was out for a moment. The swelling took a month.","ca":"車轅砸在頭之右側。當時暈了一陣。腫了一個月才消。","clue":{"en":"Head trauma eight months ago, brief loss of consciousness","zh":"八月前頭部外傷，當時短暫昏暈"},"note":"Trauma is the most direct cause of blood stasis there is, and a history like this makes the pattern almost self-evident. It also matters for a second reason: a head injury with any loss of consciousness, and any headache that has changed in character, worsened steadily, or arrived with new weakness, vomiting, fever or visual change, is referred for medical assessment. His has been unchanged for eight months and nothing new has appeared — but that is a judgement you make deliberately, not an assumption you carry. 外傷為致瘀最直捷之因，有此病史，其證幾自明。又當為第二事計：頭部外傷而曾昏暈者，及頭痛之性質改變、日漸加重、或新見肢弱、嘔吐、發熱、視物異常者，皆當轉介以求醫察。本案八月無變，亦無新見——然此為審而後定之判斷，非可默而假之。"},{"q":"Do you get dizzy, or is your temper short?","cq":"眩暈否？性躁否？","good":0,"a":"No dizziness. My temper is the same as it always was, which my wife says is not a compliment.","ca":"不眩。脾氣還是老樣子——內人說那不是誇獎。","clue":{"en":"No dizziness, no change in temper","zh":"無眩暈，情性如常"},"note":"A negative worth having. Dizziness, irritability, a red face and a wiry pulse would have made this Liver yang rising, which is the commonest cause of one-sided headache and the pattern you must actively exclude here. He has none of it. 陰性所見亦有其用。若見眩暈、易怒、面赤、脈弦，則當責之肝陽上亢——偏頭痛之最常見者，本案所必須排除者也。本案皆無。"}],"look":[{"t":"Dark purple body with stasis patches; coat thin and unremarkable","c":"舌質紫暗有瘀斑；苔薄而無特異","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Dark purple tongue with stasis patches","zh":"舌紫暗有瘀斑"},"note":"Correct, and notice where you had to look. The coating here says nothing — thin, ordinary, no pathogen sitting on it. Everything is in the tongue <b>body</b>, which reports the state of blood and of the organs rather than the presence of an invader. A useful habit: coat for the pathogen, body for the blood and the organ. 是，且當察你所觀者何處。本案之苔無所告：薄而尋常，其上無邪。所見者盡在舌<b>質</b>——質候血與臟，苔候邪之有無。可作一法記之：察苔以知邪，察質以知血與臟。"},{"t":"Pale and thin","c":"舌淡而瘦","ok":0,"note":"Blood deficiency — and blood-deficient headache is real: dull, hollow, worse when he is tired, better for lying down and for a warm hand. His refuses the hand and gets worse at night. 血虛之舌。血虛頭痛誠有之：隱隱空痛，遇勞則甚，臥則稍安，喜溫手按之。本案拒按，且入夜而劇。"},{"t":"Red with a thin yellow coat","c":"舌紅苔薄黃","ok":0,"note":"Heat, most likely Liver yang or Liver fire rising — the pattern you specifically excluded when you asked about dizziness and temper. 主熱，多為肝陽或肝火上炎——即你問眩暈與情性時所排除者。"},{"t":"Swollen with a thick greasy coat","c":"舌胖苔厚膩","ok":0,"note":"Phlegm-damp, which gives a headache too — but a heavy one, as though the head were wrapped, with a full chest, nausea and dizziness. His is a nail, not a wrapping. 痰濕之舌，亦能作頭痛——然其痛為重，如物裹之，兼胸悶、噁心、眩暈。本案如釘而非如裹。"}],"pulse":[{"t":"Fine and choppy 細澀","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Fine choppy pulse","zh":"脈細澀"},"note":"Correct. <b>Choppy</b> is the pulse of blood that does not flow smoothly, and it is the pulse that matters here. <b>Fine</b> adds that the vessel is under-filled — eight months of pain, poor sleep and a slow appetite will do that, and it is a reminder that a long-standing excess usually has some depletion behind it by the time you meet it. 是。<b>澀</b>者血行不利之脈，本案所憑在此。<b>細</b>者兼言脈道不充——八月之痛、寐差、納減，自足致之。此亦提醒：久病之實，及見之時，其後多已有虧。"},{"t":"Wiry 弦","ok":0,"note":"Liver — constraint or rising yang. That is the differential you excluded, and the pulse is where the exclusion is easiest to confirm. Wiry has tension; choppy has friction. 主肝：或鬱或陽亢。此正你所排除之證，而其排除以脈為最易驗。弦者緊張，澀者艱滯。"},{"t":"Slippery 滑","ok":0,"note":"Phlegm, damp or food — something accumulated and rolling. His pulse catches rather than rolls. 主痰、濕、食，有形之積而往來流利。本案之脈艱滯而不流利。"},{"t":"Floating 浮","ok":0,"note":"An exterior pattern, days old. His is eight months old and began with a cart shaft. 表證之脈，病在數日。本案八月，且起於車轅。"}],"dx":[{"ask":"Step 1 — he pointed. Which channel does that place belong to?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第一步：其指所指。此處屬何經？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Shaoyang — the temple and the side of the head, ear to eyebrow","c":"少陽 — 顳部側頭，自耳上至眉際","ok":1,"note":"Correct, and it is worth learning the whole division because headache is the complaint where it pays off most. <b>Taiyang</b>: back of the head running into the nape — Bladder and Small Intestine. <b>Yangming</b>: forehead and brow-ridge — Large Intestine and Stomach. <b>Shaoyang</b>: both sides, temple to ear — Gallbladder and Triple Burner. <b>Jueyin</b>: the vertex, drawing down into the eye — Liver. Naming the channel gives you the local points, the distal points and even the guiding herbs, all from one gesture of the patient&#39;s hand. 是。頭痛之證，分經之用最著，故當全記其屬。<b>太陽</b>：後頭連項——膀胱、小腸。<b>陽明</b>：前額連眉稜——大腸、胃。<b>少陽</b>：兩側顳部連耳——膽、三焦。<b>厥陰</b>：巔頂而牽引目系——肝。經既定，則局部之穴、遠道之穴、乃至引經之藥，皆由病人一指而得。"},{"t":"Taiyang — it is a headache, and headaches are Taiyang","c":"太陽 — 凡頭痛皆屬太陽","ok":0,"note":"Taiyang owns the back of the head and the nape, not the whole skull. This is the error that leads to needling the occiput for a temporal pain and wondering why nothing changed. 太陽所主在後頭與項，非全顱也。此誤所以取後枕以治顳痛，而怪其無效。"},{"t":"Jueyin — the Liver is behind most headaches","c":"厥陰 — 頭痛多責之肝","ok":0,"note":"The Liver is behind many of them, and Jueyin headache is real — but it sits at the vertex and draws down into the eye. His is above the ear, and his hand has been telling you so since he walked in. 頭痛責肝者誠多，厥陰頭痛亦實有之——然其位在巔，牽引目系。本案在耳上，其手自入門即已言之。"},{"t":"Yangming — the front of the head","c":"陽明 — 頭之前部","ok":0,"note":"Forehead and brow-ridge. He drew his fingers backward from the temple toward the ear, not forward to the brow. 陽明所主在前額眉稜。本案自太陽向後而及耳，非向前而及眉。"}]},{"ask":"Step 2 — the channel is named. What kind of pain is it?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第二步：經既定矣。其痛屬何？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Blood stasis — boring, fixed, worse at night, after an injury, with a purple tongue","c":"血瘀 — 鑽痛、固定、夜甚、有外傷、舌紫","ok":1,"note":"Correct, and five findings agree, which is more than you usually get. The word he chose was <i>nail</i>. The place has not moved in eight months. It sharpens after dark. There is a clear traumatic cause. And the tongue is dark purple with patches. Note that the channel and the pathology are separate answers to separate questions — Shaoyang tells you <i>where</i>, stasis tells you <i>what</i>, and you need both before you can choose a single point. 是，五證同歸，較常案為多。其所擇之字曰「釘」。其處八月不移。入夜而銳。外傷之因甚明。舌紫暗而有斑。當知經與病理各為一問之答：少陽言其<b>所在</b>，血瘀言其<b>所為</b>；二者俱得，而後可定一穴。"},{"t":"Liver yang rising","c":"肝陽上亢","ok":0,"note":"The commonest cause of one-sided headache, and the one you are obliged to exclude — which you did. Liver yang brings distending pain rather than boring, dizziness, irritability, a red face, poor sleep, a wiry pulse, and it fluctuates with mood and rest. He has none of these and a clear injury instead. 偏頭痛之最常見者，亦你所必當排除者——而你已排之。肝陽者其痛為脹而非鑽，兼眩暈、易怒、面赤、寐差、脈弦，且隨情志作息而進退。本案皆無，而有明確外傷。"},{"t":"Blood deficiency failing to nourish the head","c":"血虛不能上榮","ok":0,"note":"Blood-deficient headache is dull and hollow, comes on when he is tired or after his period in a woman, improves with rest and welcomes a warm hand — and the tongue is pale, not purple. Note the pair: too little blood and blood that has stopped moving both involve blood, and the tongue tells them apart at a glance. 血虛頭痛隱隱而空，遇勞則作，婦人多於經後，得息則減，喜溫手按之；其舌淡而不紫。當記此對：血少與血止皆病在血，而舌一望可別。"},{"t":"Phlegm-damp clouding the head","c":"痰濕蒙蔽清竅","ok":0,"note":"That headache is heavy — the head feels wrapped or capped — and travels with a full chest, nausea, dizziness, a swollen tongue and a thick greasy coat. His coat is thin and his pain is a nail. 痰濕之頭痛為重，如裹如蒙，兼胸悶、噁心、眩暈、舌胖苔厚膩。本案苔薄，其痛如釘。"}]},{"ask":"Step 3 — a headache this old. What else do you owe the patient before you needle?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第三步：頭痛歷久如此。未針之前，尚有何事當為？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Establish that it has not changed — no new symptoms, no worsening, no change in character","c":"確認其未變 — 無新見、無漸劇、性質未改","ok":1,"note":"Correct, and it takes one minute. A stable, unchanging headache after a known injury is one thing; a headache that has changed character, is steadily worsening, wakes him from sleep as a new development, or arrives with new weakness, numbness, vomiting, fever, neck stiffness or visual change is another, and belongs with a physician the same day. His has been the same for eight months with nothing new. You may proceed — and you ask this again at every visit, because <i>unchanged for eight months</i> is only true until it is not. 是，此不過一分鐘之事。已知外傷之後，其痛穩而不變者，一事也；若其性質已改、日漸加重、新見痛醒、或兼新起之肢弱、麻木、嘔吐、發熱、項強、視物異常者，又一事也，當日即須就醫。本案八月如一，無所新見，可施治。然每診必復問之——「八月不變」一語，只在其未變之前為真。"},{"t":"Nothing — the pattern is clear, so treat it","c":"無他 — 證已明，治之可也","ok":0,"note":"The pattern <i>is</i> clear. That is not the same as the patient being safe to treat here, and the two questions are answered separately. Pattern differentiation tells you how; screening tells you whether. 證誠明矣。然「證明」與「此人宜於此室受治」非一事，二問各自為答。辨證所以定其法，篩查所以定其可否。"},{"t":"Take a full pulse and tongue record, and nothing more","c":"詳記舌脈而已","ok":0,"note":"Good practice, and not the question. A tongue and pulse record is documentation of the pattern; it does not screen for what a pattern cannot see. 記錄誠善，然非此問。舌脈之錄，所記者證也；證所不能見者，非錄可代。"},{"t":"Ask him to stop work until the pain resolves","c":"令其停工，俟痛已而後作","ok":0,"note":"Kind, impractical, and not a safety measure. A wheelwright who stops working does not eat. Advise on posture and breaks at the lathe if you like; the actual duty here is to know what would make you send him elsewhere. 其意甚厚，而勢有不能，且非安全之計。車匠輟工則無食。可教以俯身之法與作息之節；然此處所當盡者，在知何等見症當遣之他就。"}]}],"rx":[{"id":"GB8","t":"Shu&#242;g&#468; GB8 率谷","ok":1,"note":"A Gallbladder point on the side of the head, sitting in the exact area his finger kept returning to — the local point for a one-sided temporal headache. Local points on the head are usually threaded along the skin rather than perpendicular, which is a technique worth noticing here. 足少陽之穴，在側頭，正當其指屢按之處——偏頭痛顳部之局部要穴。頭部局穴多沿皮平刺而不直刺，此法於本案尤當留意。"},{"id":"GB34","t":"Y&#225;ngl&#237;ngqu&#225;n GB34 陽陵泉","ok":1,"note":"Sea point of the Gallbladder — the distal point of the same channel, at the far end of the line his pain is drawn along. Pairing a local point on the head with a distal point on the leg of the same channel is the standard shape of a channel-differentiated treatment. 膽之合穴，同經之遠道穴，在其痛所循之線之另一端。頭取局部、足取遠道，同經相配，此即分經論治之常法。"},{"id":"LR3","t":"T&#224;ich&#333;ng LR3 太衝","ok":1,"note":"Source point of the Liver. The Liver stores blood, and Liver and Gallbladder are an interior-exterior pair, so this reaches both the blood and the channel. Paired with LI4 it makes the Four Gates, the classical combination for moving qi and blood through the whole body — useful in a stasis case that has lasted eight months. 肝之原穴。肝藏血，肝膽相表裡，故一穴而及血與經。配合谷為「四關」，古法所以行一身之氣血——本案瘀已八月，正宜之。"},{"id":"KI7","t":"F&#249;li&#363; KI7 復溜","ok":0,"note":"Warms Kidney yang and moves water. Nothing in this case is cold, wet or deficient in yang. 溫腎陽、行停水。本案無寒、無濕、無陽虛。"},{"id":"SP9","t":"Y&#299;nl&#237;ngqu&#225;n SP9 陰陵泉","ok":0,"note":"Yesterday&#39;s point, for draining damp. His coat is thin, his head is not heavy, and there is nothing to drain. 昨日之穴，主利濕。本案苔薄、頭不重，無濕可利。"},{"id":"LU5","t":"Ch&#464;z&#233; LU5 尺澤","ok":0,"note":"Clears Lung heat downward. Wrong organ, wrong direction, wrong pattern. 清肺熱而下行。臟非、向非、證非。"}],"tech":[{"t":"Reducing method, threading the head point along the skin","c":"瀉法，頭穴沿皮平刺","ok":1,"note":"<b>Correct on both counts, and the second half is a safety habit as much as a technique.</b> Reduce, because eight months of fixed stabbing pain that refuses pressure is an excess. And on the skull, needle obliquely or transversely along the skin rather than perpendicular — there is bone directly beneath and very little tissue above it, so threading is both safer and, at points like this one, more effective. 二者皆是，而後半既為手法，亦為安全之習。瀉者，八月固定刺痛而拒按，實也。頭顱之穴，當斜刺或沿皮平刺而不直刺——其下即骨，其上肌肉甚薄，故平刺既安且於此類穴為效。"},{"t":"Reducing method, perpendicular insertion at the head point","c":"瀉法，頭穴直刺","ok":0,"note":"The technique is right and the angle is not. Perpendicular needling over the skull meets bone almost immediately; it is uncomfortable, it achieves nothing extra, and on the head the transverse thread is the standard approach for a reason. 法是而角度非。顱上直刺，一入即抵骨，徒增其痛而無所增益。頭部沿皮透刺為常法，其故在此。"},{"t":"Reinforcing method — the pulse is fine, so he is depleted","c":"補法 — 脈細，其人已虧","ok":0,"note":"The fine pulse is real and worth remembering for later. But the presenting problem is a blockage that refuses pressure, and supplementing into a blocked channel makes stasis pain worse before it makes anything better. Support the blood after you have moved it, not instead. 脈細誠有，且當記之以為後圖。然目前所苦為阻而拒按；塞而補之，瘀痛先劇而後未必有功。當先行其血，而後養之，不可以養代行。"},{"t":"Reducing with generous moxa on the head point","c":"瀉法，頭穴重灸","ok":0,"note":"Moxa does move blood, and there is no heat here to forbid it outright — but generous moxa directly on the temporal region is poor practice: the skin is thin, hair is present, and the risk of a burn is real. If warmth is wanted, warm the distal points. 灸誠能行血，本案亦無熱以絕之。然顳部重灸則失於工：其膚薄、有髮，灼傷之虞非虛。若欲取其溫，當灸遠道之穴。"}]};
